body:
This PR fixes the issue with map overlays in embed mode for all visibility types (public, members-only, and paid-only).

### The Problem:
The previous approach only worked for public posts in embed mode. For members-only and paid-only posts, the embed mode wasn't properly bypassing the content restrictions, resulting in missing map overlays.

### The Solution:
1. Store the original post content in a hidden div that's always included in the page:
   ```html
   <div id="original-content" style="display: none;">{{content}}</div>
   ```

2. In embed mode, retrieve this content and use it to replace the restricted content:
   ```javascript
   // Get the original content
   const originalContent = document.getElementById('original-content').innerHTML;

   // Create the map HTML with the original content
   const mapHtml = `
     <article class="post-full leaflet-map-template map-template">
         <div id="map" style="height: 100vh;"></div>
         <div class="map-data-container">${originalContent}</div>
     </article>
   `;

   // Replace members-only or paid-only content with the map
   if (membersContent) {
     membersContent.innerHTML = mapHtml;
   } else if (paidContent) {
     paidContent.innerHTML = mapHtml;
   }
   ```

3. Added additional debug logging to help diagnose any issues:
   ```javascript
   console.log("Map initialized with dimensions:", w, "x", h);
   console.log("Map data container:", document.querySelector('.map-data-container'));

   // Check if we have map data
   const mapDataContainer = document.querySelector('.map-data-container');
   if (mapDataContainer) {
     const preElements = mapDataContainer.querySelectorAll('pre');
     console.log("Found pre elements:", preElements.length);

     if (preElements.length === 0) {
       console.warn("No pre elements found in map data container");
       console.log("Map data container content:", mapDataContainer.innerHTML);
     }
   }
   ```

This approach ensures that:
1. The original post content (including JSON data for map overlays) is always available in the page
2. In embed mode, this content is used to replace the restricted content, bypassing the visibility restrictions
3. The map overlays are properly loaded for all visibility types in embed mode

### Testing:
- The map should now display overlays correctly in embed mode for all visibility types
- The embed bypass functionality should work for public, members-only, and paid-only content
- All other map functionality should remain unchanged

